  "summary": "Inspired by classic street food traditions, this savory <b>Vietnamese crispy flatbread</b> highlights the complex umami depth of fermented rice batter and creamy fermented tofu. The batter undergoes a gentle fermentation process that imparts a pleasant subtle tang, which combines with smooth coconut milk and earthy turmeric for a vibrant yellow hue and crisp texture upon cooking. Ladled thinly onto a piping hot skillet, the batter sizzles immediately, forming lacey golden edges that stay light and crispy. Inside the folded flatbread, a spread of mashed fermented tofu provides a rich, pungent savoriness balanced by sweet crunch from raw bean sprouts and tender cooked mung beans. Freshly sliced scallions and spicy chili peppers add aromatic heat, while cilantro leaves offer a cooling herb contrast. Finished with a splash of fresh lime juice right before eating, each crispy fold offers a harmonious contrast of hot, tangy, crunchy, and savory sensations that elevate simple ingredients into an extraordinary plant-focused dish.",
